	<item>
		<title>Why Your Google Pmax Ads Campaigns Are Failing</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/video/why-your-google-pmax-ads-campaigns-are-failing/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 04:49:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=video&#038;p=4436</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this video, I expose the BIGGEST mistake marketers make when running ads and how it’s draining your budget! 😱 Spoiler: It’s all about having a clear objective and NOT getting lost in Google’s endless optimization prompts. 💡 Today’s digital world is full of distractions, and Google’s constant recommendations can easily pull you away from [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-your-google-pmax-ads-campaigns-are-failing/">Why Your Google Pmax Ads Campaigns Are Failing</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4436" class="elementor elementor-4436" data-elementor-post-type="video">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d4e7c5e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="d4e7c5e" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d5e774c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="d5e774c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p><strong>In this video, I expose the BIGGEST mistake marketers make when running ads and how it’s draining your budget! <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f631.png" alt="😱" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong></p><p>Spoiler: It’s all about having a <strong>clear objective</strong> and NOT getting lost in Google’s endless optimization prompts. <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4a1.png" alt="💡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></p><p>Today’s digital world is full of distractions, and Google’s constant recommendations can easily pull you away from your core goals. In this video, I break down the powerful <strong>OKR system (Objectives and Key Results)</strong>—the strategy used by tech giants like Google, Microsoft, and LinkedIn—and show you how to apply it to your campaigns for <strong>real growth and revenue</strong>.</p><h4><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f511.png" alt="🔑" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> You’ll learn:</h4><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> How to set <strong>laser-focused objectives</strong> that align with your business goals<br /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> The secret to turning your Google Ads (especially <strong>PMax campaigns</strong>) into a <strong>sales-driving machine</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4b8.png" alt="💸" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><br /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/2705.png" alt="✅" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> How to stop <strong>wasting budget</strong> on low-impact areas and finally <strong>crush your targets</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f680.png" alt="🚀" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></p><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4ac.png" alt="💬" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong>Drop a comment below</strong> if you&#8217;ve ever felt lost in Google’s endless optimization suggestions! How do you set your objectives? I’d love to hear your thoughts.</p><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f44d.png" alt="👍" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong>Like this video?</strong> Smash that <strong>thumbs up</strong> and make sure to <strong>subscribe</strong> for more actionable tips on growing your business through smart marketing strategies. Don’t miss out!</p><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4e5.png" alt="📥" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong>Want a deeper dive?</strong> Download my free eBook <strong>&#8220;Taming PMax for eCommerce: Your Guide to Cutting Costs and Driving Profits&#8221;</strong> here: <a href="https://feedops.com/taming-pmax-for-e..." target="_new" rel="noopener">https://feedops.com/taming-pmax-for-e&#8230;</a></p><p><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4f2.png" alt="📲" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <strong>Watch now</strong> and let’s turn your ads into <strong>cash machines!</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4b0.png" alt="💰" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-your-google-pmax-ads-campaigns-are-failing/">Why Your Google Pmax Ads Campaigns Are Failing</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Why Data Feed Optimization Matters</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/video/why-data-feed-optimization-matters/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 04:40:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=video&#038;p=4434</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this insightful interview, Frank Grasso, CEO and Founder of FeedOps, dives into the critical role of data feed optimization in today&#8217;s competitive ecommerce landscape. While many ecommerce marketers know how to connect their product data to channels like Google Shopping, Frank explains why simply connecting isn’t enough. Learn how optimizing your product data can [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-data-feed-optimization-matters/">Why Data Feed Optimization Matters</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4434" class="elementor elementor-4434" data-elementor-post-type="video">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-01e700d e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="01e700d" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ff7d5b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="ff7d5b7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow"><div class="min-h-8 text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words text-start [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="75dd7c8a-ad57-42b0-a36f-4e282bfccc78" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p><strong>In this insightful interview, Frank Grasso, CEO and Founder of FeedOps, dives into the critical role of data feed optimization in today&#8217;s competitive ecommerce landscape.</strong></p><p>While many ecommerce marketers know how to connect their product data to channels like Google Shopping, Frank explains why simply connecting isn’t enough. Learn how optimizing your product data can significantly enhance your digital marketing strategy, driving more relevant traffic, improving SEO for ecommerce, and boosting your marketing ROI.</p><p>Frank discusses the importance of ensuring your products are accurately and attractively presented to stand out in a saturated market. Whether you&#8217;re looking to improve your online advertising efforts or seeking to maximize the effectiveness of your ecommerce marketing, this video offers valuable insights that can help you achieve better results.</p></div></div></div></div>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-data-feed-optimization-matters/">Why Data Feed Optimization Matters</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>How I Learned Google Ads Is Selling, Not Just Advertising</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/video/how-i-learned-google-ads-is-selling-not-just-advertising/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 02:35:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=video&#038;p=4419</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Frank Grasso&#8217;s Early Realization in Digital Marketing In this video, digital marketing expert Frank Grasso reflects on a pivotal moment from his early career. Initially confident in his advertising strategies, Frank believed he had identified the ineffective portions of his campaigns. However, after years of managing Google Ads, he realized that he wasn&#8217;t merely advertising; [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/how-i-learned-google-ads-is-selling-not-just-advertising/">How I Learned Google Ads Is Selling, Not Just Advertising</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4419" class="elementor elementor-4419" data-elementor-post-type="video">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-fe17549 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="fe17549" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-10d07ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="10d07ee" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p><strong>Frank Grasso&#8217;s Early Realization in Digital Marketing</strong></p><p>In this video, digital marketing expert Frank Grasso reflects on a pivotal moment from his early career. Initially confident in his advertising strategies, Frank believed he had identified the ineffective portions of his campaigns. However, after years of managing Google Ads, he realized that he wasn&#8217;t merely advertising; he was actively selling.</p><p><strong>Distinguishing Between Advertising and Selling</strong></p><p>This insight led Frank to explore the nuanced distinction between advertising and selling, fundamentally altering his approach to digital marketing. Advertising aims to build brand awareness and shape consumer perceptions, while selling focuses directly on driving transactions and achieving a measurable Return on Ad Spend (ROAS).</p><p><strong>The Role of Google&#8217;s Performance Max (PMax) Campaigns</strong></p><p>A prime example of this convergence is Google&#8217;s Performance Max (PMax) campaigns. PMax is a goal-based campaign type that allows advertisers to access all of Google&#8217;s channels—Search, Display, YouTube, Gmail, and more—through a single campaign. It utilizes machine learning to optimize performance in real-time across these channels.</p><p><strong>Blurring the Lines Between Brand Advertising and Performance Advertising</strong></p><p>While PMax offers the advantage of expansive reach and automated optimization, it also blurs the lines between brand advertising and performance advertising. By automating placements and creatives across various channels, PMax integrates brand messaging with direct sales tactics, making it challenging to distinguish between efforts aimed at brand building and those focused on immediate sales.</p><p><strong>The Importance of Understanding This Blend for Marketers</strong></p><p>Understanding this blend is crucial for marketers. Recognizing how PMax intertwines brand advertising with performance selling can lead to more informed decisions, ensuring that campaigns are aligned with overarching marketing objectives.</p><p><strong>Reflecting on the Transformative Understanding</strong></p><p>Reflecting on his journey, Frank emphasizes that acknowledging the dual role of platforms like PMax has been transformative. By understanding this convergence, he has crafted strategies that effectively balance brand development with direct sales goals.</p><p><strong>About Frank Grasso</strong></p><p>Frank Grasso is the Chief Executive Officer of FeedOps, an ad tech company specializing in product data, ad automation, and artificial intelligence to create and optimize advertising assets. With over 25 years of experience in digital marketing, Frank has been recognized for his innovative approach and leadership. He has authored works focusing on practical strategies for e-commerce and agency growth, including &#8220;The Ultimate Guide To Profit From Pmax (Google Shopping)&#8221; and &#8220;How To Grow And Scale A Digital Agency.&#8221;</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/how-i-learned-google-ads-is-selling-not-just-advertising/">How I Learned Google Ads Is Selling, Not Just Advertising</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Why Product Types in Google and Microsoft Matter</title>
		<link>https://feedops.com/video/why-product-types-in-google-and-microsoft-matter/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jazib Zaidi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 02 Feb 2025 17:00:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://feedops.com/?post_type=learn&#038;p=4390</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Optimize Product Types in Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers This video guide explains how to refine product types to boost your organic shopping visibility and PPC performance in both Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers. Refine Your Product Categorization for Google and Microsoft Adjust your product hierarchy to target ready-to-buy consumers on Google and Microsoft. For [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-product-types-in-google-and-microsoft-matter/">Why Product Types in Google and Microsoft Matter</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="4390" class="elementor elementor-4390" data-elementor-post-type="video">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-bd54b3d e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent" data-id="bd54b3d" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-edfe1d3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="edfe1d3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<h2><strong>Optimize Product Types in Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers</strong></h2><p>This video guide explains how to refine product types to boost your organic shopping visibility and PPC performance in both Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers.</p><h3><strong>Refine Your Product Categorization for Google and Microsoft</strong></h3><p>Adjust your product hierarchy to target ready-to-buy consumers on Google and Microsoft. For example, using a detailed structure like:</p><ul><li><strong>Clothing &gt; Women’s Clothing &gt; Dresses &gt; Maxi Dresses &gt; Summer Maxi Dresses</strong></li></ul><p>helps optimize long-tail keywords such as &#8220;summer maxi dresses under $100&#8221; on both Google and Microsoft.</p><h3><strong>Benefits of Detailed Product Types in Google and Microsoft</strong></h3><p>This approach offers several advantages for both Google and Microsoft:</p><ul><li>It increases click-through rates.</li><li>It reduces competition.</li><li>It improves your Return on Ad Spend (ROAS).</li></ul><h3><strong>Enhance Search Relevance in Google and Microsoft</strong></h3><p>Google’s Merchant Center Help documentation stresses the need for detailed product types. Microsoft also supports detailed categorization for better ad relevance. By integrating Level 5 product details into your titles, you capture a wider range of relevant searches. For example, a title such as:</p><p>&#8220;Claire Glamour | V-Neck Long Evening Dress &#8211; Small Blue Summer Maxi Dress&#8221;</p><p>creates precise keywords that boost visibility in Google and Microsoft search results.</p><h3><strong>Advanced Strategies for Google and Microsoft</strong></h3><p>Boost your performance on Google and Microsoft by:</p><ul><li>Creating labels for products within specific types and price ranges.</li><li>Enabling targeted campaigns for high-converting keywords.</li></ul><p>These tactics help lower your cost per click and increase sales effectiveness on both platforms.</p><h3><strong>Simplify with FeedOps for Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers</strong></h3><p><a href="https://feedops.com/">FeedOps</a> streamlines the process of refining product types and managing custom labels for both Google and Microsoft. Whether you are new to eCommerce or seeking to optimize your store, you can find valuable tools and insights at FeedOps.com.</p><p>Maximize your eCommerce performance today by leveraging detailed product types in both Google and Microsoft Merchant Centers!</p>								</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<p>The post <a href="https://feedops.com/video/why-product-types-in-google-and-microsoft-matter/">Why Product Types in Google and Microsoft Matter</a> appeared first on <a href="https://feedops.com">FeedOps</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
